config BENCHMARK_AUTO_DUT
	bool "Run the benchmark batch autonomously after boot (Device B / DUT on PPK II)"
	help
	  The DUT initializes, advertises, accepts the pairing of Device A and,
	  once Device A has subscribed, sends all payload sizes from
	  auto_benchmark.c on its own. The results are sent to Device A over the
	  results characteristic, so the DUT's serial terminal is never needed.
	  Build with -DEXTRA_CONF_FILE=auto_dut.conf.

config BENCHMARK_IDLE_TEST
	bool "Idle current test: step through sleep / timer / BLE phases (Device B on PPK II)"
	depends on !BENCHMARK_AUTO_DUT && SOC_COMPATIBLE_NRF52X
	help
	  Measures what the benchmark timer and Bluetooth add to the idle current.
	  See src/idle_test.c, evaluate with data_processing/idle_test.py.
	  Build with -DEXTRA_CONF_FILE=idle_test.conf.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"